WEBVTT

00:01.383 --> 00:03.927
<i>Think you can
track 'em down, Melone?</i>

00:04.136 --> 00:05.137
Yeah.

00:06.597 --> 00:08.890
I've got myself a bit of blood…

00:10.059 --> 00:11.769
Bucciarati's, that is.

00:12.561 --> 00:15.105
Hey, when's this piece of junk
gonna get moving?

00:15.189 --> 00:16.773
Please forgive us for the delay.

00:16.857 --> 00:19.442
A replacement driver is on his way
at this very moment!

00:19.485 --> 00:21.195
What? What happened
to that other guy?

00:21.237 --> 00:23.447
Miseria,
I can't take this nonsense.

00:23.531 --> 00:25.074
Can't the parents do something
about that wailing?

00:25.533 --> 00:27.618
I knew I shouldn't have
even considered

00:27.701 --> 00:29.619
riding with these riffraff.

00:29.870 --> 00:30.871
Hey, there.

00:31.539 --> 00:33.666
You in decent physical shape?

00:33.749 --> 00:36.460
H-Hey, what do you think
you're doing?!

00:36.544 --> 00:38.629
You are sitting in
my private cabin!

00:38.671 --> 00:41.465
Open your eyes and read
what's written on the damn door.

00:45.177 --> 00:47.554
Got anything with
your date of birth written on it?

00:47.596 --> 00:48.638
Uh…

00:48.806 --> 00:49.807
Oh.

00:50.099 --> 00:52.309
Hey! What the hell are you doing?!

00:53.435 --> 00:57.439
Born March 10, 1977.
Twenty-four years old.

00:58.232 --> 01:00.651
Motto… bellissimo.

01:00.734 --> 01:01.860
Excellent vintage.

01:01.944 --> 01:03.820
Get your grubby hands off
my property!

01:03.904 --> 01:04.988
Get out!

01:05.197 --> 01:06.823
SMACK

01:07.199 --> 01:09.159
Very nice…

01:09.535 --> 01:10.953
Such stinging force.

01:10.995 --> 01:14.081
That very zesty slap you let loose
there proves without a doubt…

01:14.164 --> 01:16.291
You are…

01:16.333 --> 01:17.917
in more than decent condition.

01:18.627 --> 01:20.003
Sublime.

01:20.796 --> 01:22.589
And judging from
your delicious digits,

01:22.631 --> 01:24.090
I'd say your blood type is O.

01:24.425 --> 01:25.342
Right?

01:25.384 --> 01:27.552
Who the hell are you,
some kind of pickpocket?

01:27.636 --> 01:29.262
Who do you think I am?

01:29.305 --> 01:32.766
- I come from a very—
- Ah, I don't need your name.

01:32.933 --> 01:35.310
I don't give a shit about
your pedigree either.

01:35.352 --> 01:37.854
What's absolutely crucial is
your health condition,

01:37.938 --> 01:40.106
date of birth, and blood type.

01:41.692 --> 01:43.527
A Pisces and type O!

01:43.611 --> 01:45.738
Bucciarati is an Aries and type A,

01:45.821 --> 01:47.239
which means the two of you are

01:47.323 --> 01:48.991
completely and utterly
incompatible.

01:49.158 --> 01:51.910
This is perfection… This is divine!

01:52.161 --> 01:54.163
Looks like you're not against
drinking and smoking.

01:54.204 --> 01:55.455
Do you do any drugs?

01:55.623 --> 01:57.166
If you're into narcotics…

01:57.249 --> 02:00.752
- Then there's nothing more to say
- If this is about money, take it…

02:00.836 --> 02:02.712
- then di motto bene!
- You can even take my credit card

02:02.755 --> 02:03.922
- Listen.
- If you want…

02:04.548 --> 02:06.675
Could you just shut your nob
and listen up?

02:06.925 --> 02:08.343
How you answer the next question

02:08.385 --> 02:10.053
will determine
the success of all this.

02:10.262 --> 02:13.181
This is a question of
personal preference.

02:13.223 --> 02:14.974
Which would you personally fancy?

02:15.100 --> 02:17.560
Did you know that
the ancient Indian Sanskrit text

02:17.645 --> 02:19.563
known as the Kama Sutra

02:19.647 --> 02:23.108
includes more than
forty-eight erotic positions?

02:23.317 --> 02:26.236
And one cannot underestimate
their importance…

02:26.528 --> 02:30.365
It is the crucial first step
in creating a stellar child.

02:31.033 --> 02:32.701
Now, choose.

02:37.039 --> 02:38.415
Babyhead!

02:38.499 --> 02:40.292
H-H-Help me!

02:40.709 --> 02:41.710
Help me!

02:44.171 --> 02:45.380
CONCEPTION COMPLETE

02:45.422 --> 02:46.464
3 MINUTES UNTIL BIRTH

02:46.757 --> 02:50.469
ANALYZING DNA HARVESTED
FROM BRUNO BUCCIARATI.
MERGE WITH HOST DNA FOR
INCUBATION AND TRACKING?

02:49.927 --> 02:52.242
Oh, you're gonna be a star…

02:50.552 --> 02:52.220
1: YES. 2: NO.

02:52.388 --> 02:54.556
a demonic, vicious star.

02:58.727 --> 03:00.687
Di motto…

03:12.658 --> 03:17.158
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

03:17.996 --> 03:21.457
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

03:23.252 --> 03:27.752
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

03:28.424 --> 03:32.261
<i>But I will never give in</i>

03:32.302 --> 03:36.802
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

03:44.106 --> 03:48.606
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

03:57.161 --> 04:01.661
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

04:03.125 --> 04:07.625
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

04:10.215 --> 04:13.343
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

04:13.427 --> 04:17.927
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

04:18.640 --> 04:23.140
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

04:32.780 --> 04:37.201
EPISODE 17
BABYHEAD

04:38.911 --> 04:40.287
As long as no one finds us,

04:40.412 --> 04:43.039
we should make it to Venice
by tomorrow or the day after.

04:49.963 --> 04:51.589
Gee whiz…

04:51.673 --> 04:53.091
What's with all the doom and gloom

04:53.175 --> 04:54.634
weighing everyone down
all of a sudden?

04:55.093 --> 04:59.097
Did Bucciarati say something
to Trish to make her mad?

04:59.181 --> 05:01.975
No…
I think Trish is in a weird place

05:02.017 --> 05:03.727
precisely because
Bucciarati is staying quiet.

05:04.186 --> 05:06.062
<i>Trish is in the beginning phases of</i>

05:06.146 --> 05:08.064
<i>coming to terms
with her innate powers.</i>

05:08.190 --> 05:10.066
<i>And then,
there's her enigmatic father…</i>

05:10.442 --> 05:12.861
<i>Obviously, she has a lot
on her mind right now</i>

05:13.403 --> 05:15.905
<i>Bucciarati has his hands tied</i>

05:15.989 --> 05:18.574
<i>when it comes to bringing
anything up like that though.</i>

05:19.034 --> 05:22.829
<i>I've got to somehow learn
more about her powers.</i>

05:22.871 --> 05:25.248
<i>They've got to shine some light on
who the boss really is.</i>

05:26.667 --> 05:28.877
Her strength is nothing short
of amazing.

05:29.294 --> 05:31.045
Never once has she caved
or shed a tear.

05:32.005 --> 05:33.256
Mista!

05:33.298 --> 05:37.798
Tell Number Two and Number Three
to share the hamburger with us!

05:38.887 --> 05:40.972
Huh? What are you talking about?

05:41.056 --> 05:43.433
There's nothing to eat here
right now…

05:43.851 --> 05:44.560
Huh?

05:44.560 --> 05:47.020
Where the hell did you get that?!

05:47.229 --> 05:48.605
D-Don't tell me…

05:49.731 --> 05:52.734
Where the hell did my hamburger go?

05:54.194 --> 05:56.112
There's something under the seat.

05:56.238 --> 05:57.239
Sh-Shit!

05:57.990 --> 05:58.991
A turtle?

06:00.367 --> 06:01.951
There's something on its back…

06:01.994 --> 06:04.121
- It's got some kind of weird jewel on it…
- What are we going to do, Mista?

06:04.204 --> 06:06.039
- This a key?
- Something tells me this is real bad.

06:12.462 --> 06:13.379
What's going on now?

06:13.422 --> 06:15.715
Mista, you were supposed to have
your eyes glued on the ceiling.

06:15.757 --> 06:16.758
So what the hell happened?

06:16.758 --> 06:17.842
Huh? Me?

06:18.051 --> 06:20.845
You're asking the wrong person…

06:20.929 --> 06:22.805
That was the one moment
I wasn't looking…

06:22.848 --> 06:27.348
Huh? Maybe the truck stopped…

06:30.397 --> 06:32.023
BIRTHING SUCCESSFUL

06:37.070 --> 06:38.863
Ow!

06:39.281 --> 06:40.824
What happened?

06:41.283 --> 06:42.701
Th-This…

06:42.784 --> 06:44.660
D-Don't tell me I—

06:46.121 --> 06:49.666
That's a relief,
I'm perfectly fine.

06:49.708 --> 06:51.668
Cazzo, goddamn nutcase!

06:51.710 --> 06:54.421
What was that about?
Dirty, perverted sicko!

06:54.463 --> 06:57.466
Think you can scare me and
live to tell the freakin' tale?!

06:57.633 --> 07:00.510
I'll freakin' murder you!

07:00.636 --> 07:01.637
Piece of shit stronzo!

07:01.678 --> 07:04.597
Hello? Are you the conductor
of this train?

07:04.640 --> 07:06.099
I don't care what you're doing.

07:06.141 --> 07:07.684
Drop everything and
come to my cabin now!

07:10.103 --> 07:11.229
WHAT DOES "FREAKIN MURDER" MEAN?

07:12.648 --> 07:14.316
Looks like we got a baby.

07:14.608 --> 07:17.193
Mother dearest is already
imparting her wisdom too.

07:17.486 --> 07:19.654
To Babyhead's child, that is…

07:19.780 --> 07:21.031
Fantastico!

07:21.114 --> 07:24.408
He's already responding to mama's
petulantly violent inclinations!

07:24.493 --> 07:26.870
Remember, mother knows best!

07:27.245 --> 07:30.414
Listen, I was assaulted
by some pervert…

07:30.499 --> 07:31.750
Can you believe it? Me!

07:31.833 --> 07:33.167
Clearly, your private cabins
aren't private

07:33.210 --> 07:34.878
'cause the shitty locks
can't keep people out!

07:34.920 --> 07:36.838
Look at the welt he gave me!

07:37.172 --> 07:38.590
Ugh, I could scream!

07:38.674 --> 07:41.760
That pezzo di merda… Get ready,
there's gonna be a take down!

07:41.843 --> 07:44.428
- What does…"murder" mean?
- You're gonna pay out the ass for this…

07:44.513 --> 07:47.015
- What does…"pezzo di merda" mean?
- This is ludicrous!

07:47.766 --> 07:49.267
Shall we crack the books?

07:49.351 --> 07:51.102
Okay, pay close attention.

07:51.186 --> 07:55.064
This is Mr. Lion.
He's the king of the jungle.

07:55.148 --> 07:56.649
The one with the long nose
is Mr. Elephant,

07:56.692 --> 07:58.735
and the one with the long neck
is Mr. Giraffe.

07:58.902 --> 08:01.362
The one nibbling the grass
is Mr. Zebra.

08:01.405 --> 08:02.739
And…

08:03.240 --> 08:04.491
Oh, what's this?

08:04.533 --> 08:07.619
This is what the word murder means.
Does that make sense?

08:07.703 --> 08:10.539
It means to kill or
to put an end to.

08:10.998 --> 08:14.418
Next… Oh, looky here,
these are what kids play with.

08:15.043 --> 08:17.587
This is what's called a top,
and this is baseball.

08:17.879 --> 08:21.173
This is bowling,
and these are ice skates.

08:23.427 --> 08:27.264
Ooh, look at all the fun things
you can do with them…

08:27.597 --> 08:29.807
These dead-looking guys
are pezzi di merda.

08:29.891 --> 08:31.267
You kill one pezzo di merda,

08:31.309 --> 08:34.312
but you kill two or more
pezzi di merda.

08:34.396 --> 08:35.647
This making sense?

08:35.731 --> 08:39.443
But the way in which you kill
is completely up to you.

08:39.943 --> 08:41.903
Just remember,
you are under no circumstances

08:41.945 --> 08:43.780
to do any harm
to this girl named Trish.

08:43.864 --> 08:45.448
You are to capture her,
not kill her.

08:45.657 --> 08:46.908
There will also be a new guy

08:46.950 --> 08:48.952
whose face you will have
never seen before.

08:48.994 --> 08:50.870
He'll be with Bucciarati,

08:50.912 --> 08:53.164
so you'll need to seek them both
out and put an end to them.

08:53.206 --> 08:55.333
I GOTTA GO PEE PEE.
WHAT SHOULD I DO?

08:56.001 --> 08:57.502
What should you do?

08:58.003 --> 08:59.754
Just answer nature's call.

08:59.796 --> 09:01.964
Going pee-pee is what babies do.

09:02.049 --> 09:04.968
But it doesn't look like
the lock's been broken…

09:05.010 --> 09:06.928
H-Hey, what is this?!

09:07.262 --> 09:08.805
Now you've got some kind of shit
leaking on me

09:08.889 --> 09:10.307
from this third-rate train's roof!

09:10.348 --> 09:12.058
I'm sorry, but I don't…

09:12.809 --> 09:14.060
I-It reeks!

09:14.102 --> 09:16.771
What is this?!
It's so vile and disgusting!

09:16.813 --> 09:17.980
Signora…

09:18.273 --> 09:22.773
MOMMY IS YELLING AT ME
AND IS SAYING THAT I REEK
AND THAT I AM VILE AND DISGUSTING.

09:19.816 --> 09:24.316
It appear so.
Then what would you say about her?

09:25.363 --> 09:27.323
I'VE GOT THE BEST MOMMY
IN THE WORLD.

09:26.448 --> 09:27.323
Yes!

09:27.365 --> 09:29.742
Di motto! Fantabulous!

09:29.785 --> 09:31.327
You're such a good little student!

09:31.286 --> 09:33.246
I'M HUNGRY…
WHAT SHOULD I DO?

09:34.539 --> 09:38.167
That'll come soon enough.
You still have much to learn.

09:38.210 --> 09:39.085
It's too soon.

09:39.086 --> 09:40.545
GIVE ME SOMETHING TO DRINK,
PLEASE LET ME HAVE A DRINK!

09:40.962 --> 09:43.255
Hey, not yet! I told you, not yet!

09:43.298 --> 09:44.966
I can't take this anymore!

09:45.008 --> 09:47.176
I can't spend another second
on this train!

09:47.219 --> 09:50.639
I will sue, and this train company
will be held accountable!

09:50.931 --> 09:54.059
How do I know this bump isn't
the result of a serious fracture…?

10:00.690 --> 10:02.858
Huh? Why can't…?

10:06.113 --> 10:08.281
Her parenting was just too good!

10:08.323 --> 10:11.784
I mean, it's great she taught him
the importance of killing so soon,

10:11.827 --> 10:13.703
but it's too soon!

10:16.790 --> 10:17.791
H-Hey!

10:18.834 --> 10:23.171
BUCCIARATI'S DNA IS
CURRENTLY INACTIVE.
THE MATERIAL REMAINS AT REST
AT AN UNDISCLOSED LOCATION
IN THE NORTH.

10:21.461 --> 10:23.192
What am I going to do with you?

10:23.755 --> 10:26.174
Still, you sure are
a talented little bambino.

10:26.341 --> 10:28.343
Thanks to Bucciarati's DNA,

10:28.385 --> 10:31.262
automatic tracking
is well under way.

10:31.346 --> 10:32.555
You've gotta put in the work,

10:32.597 --> 10:36.225
but Babyhead's offspring is
the ultimate long-range Stand.

10:36.977 --> 10:39.396
All will tremble and die
before your greatness!

10:43.525 --> 10:45.568
MELONE
BABYHEAD

10:46.194 --> 10:49.530
- Let's just steal one already.
- Are you stupid?

10:49.573 --> 10:52.826
Yeah sure, why don't we just
announce ourselves to the enemy.

10:53.034 --> 10:55.036
They'll just ambush us and
that will be the end of that!

10:55.078 --> 10:56.746
I hate to say it, but…

10:56.830 --> 10:58.915
Fugo's got a real good point,
ragazzi.

10:58.957 --> 11:01.626
Then let's hear what
Bucciarati wants us to do.

11:03.712 --> 11:05.588
W-What are you doing, Giorno?

11:06.715 --> 11:09.426
Driving off with one of them
would be too obvious.

11:09.509 --> 11:11.761
But if we take a hundred…

11:21.104 --> 11:23.606
What do you think happens when
there's more than one car missing…

11:23.857 --> 11:27.777
and the cars that are missing are
dismantled and scattered

11:27.819 --> 11:30.029
all over the city and beyond?

11:30.071 --> 11:32.406
Tracking down the stolen cars
gets a lot more complicated,

11:32.449 --> 11:34.951
which gives us more than
enough time to get to

11:34.993 --> 11:36.452
that mysterious city of water
called Venezia.

11:36.703 --> 11:38.204
I guess that makes sense…

11:38.246 --> 11:40.623
Hitchhiking with a bunch of
creepers wouldn't be fun.

11:41.750 --> 11:42.959
Fine, it's settled.

11:45.921 --> 11:48.924
Giorno, you tell Bucciarati.

11:49.549 --> 11:50.550
Here.

11:51.009 --> 11:52.969
We're gonna go get ourselves
a brand new car.

11:54.846 --> 11:56.305
I'd like you to please
get down from the chair.

11:56.598 --> 11:58.725
It's far too dangerous for you
to be out there now.

11:58.892 --> 12:01.102
Um, well, you see, Mr. Bucciarati.

12:01.394 --> 12:03.187
It'd be great if you…

12:03.271 --> 12:04.855
Well, I have a really
dumb question,

12:04.940 --> 12:06.691
and I really hope you'll
give me an answer.

12:06.942 --> 12:08.068
What is the question?

12:08.401 --> 12:10.903
Well, to put it nicely,
what's the bathroom situation here?

12:10.946 --> 12:13.490
You aren't thinking of having me
use some kind of diaper, are you?

12:15.742 --> 12:18.536
Well of course,
that's… an understandable concern.

12:18.620 --> 12:20.955
Thank goodness…
I knew you were reasonable.

12:24.834 --> 12:26.961
The closet is now our bathroom.

12:27.212 --> 12:28.213
Go ahead.

12:28.296 --> 12:29.422
Go ahead?

12:29.589 --> 12:32.008
I'm assuming you need to use the…

12:32.342 --> 12:35.178
I honestly couldn't tell you
where this portal leads,

12:35.262 --> 12:37.055
but I'm sure the turtle
will be fine.

12:37.180 --> 12:38.639
It might actually be good for him.

12:40.100 --> 12:43.436
Nothing you're saying is
making any sense to me…

12:44.104 --> 12:46.523
Bucciarati, we've secured a car.

12:46.898 --> 12:49.525
Got it. Once we secure the area,
we can depart.

12:49.818 --> 12:51.110
Ready when you are.

12:56.700 --> 12:59.202
<i>That bike…
Where'd that come from?</i>

12:59.244 --> 13:00.703
<i>And where'd the heck
did the driver go?</i>

13:00.787 --> 13:02.914
Giorno, is something wrong?

13:06.668 --> 13:07.710
Trish?

13:21.725 --> 13:23.184
What the hell?!

13:24.311 --> 13:25.312
Trish!

13:26.354 --> 13:27.897
Miseria!

13:29.232 --> 13:30.316
Trish!

13:30.442 --> 13:31.443
Zipper—

13:33.111 --> 13:35.071
<i>Merda… It's a Stand!</i>

13:35.155 --> 13:36.906
<i>We have a long-range Stand
on our hands!</i>

13:36.948 --> 13:41.369
<i>But its power is out of control.
What's—?</i>

13:43.038 --> 13:45.665
Bucciarati,
please be extra careful.

13:45.707 --> 13:47.542
A bike appeared out of nowhere.

13:49.961 --> 13:51.170
Bucciarati?

13:54.382 --> 13:56.175
Dammit, no… Bucciarati!

13:56.217 --> 13:58.302
Where's Trish? Trish!

13:58.386 --> 14:01.222
<i>I had the turtle the entire time…</i>

14:01.264 --> 14:03.474
<i>There's no way I wouldn't have seen
the two of them exit.</i>

14:03.558 --> 14:06.769
<i>Could something have already
got them right from under my nose?</i>

14:06.936 --> 14:08.771
Golden Wind!

14:11.358 --> 14:12.776
Di motto!

14:12.776 --> 14:15.487
TRISH HAS BEEN ACQUIRED.
BUCCIARATI IS CURRENTLY
ALSO IN CAPTIVITY.
WHAT NOW, MASTER?

14:15.570 --> 14:18.864
Di motto! Bravissimo, Babyhead!

14:18.907 --> 14:21.284
Now use that head of yours and
make yourself scarce!

14:21.326 --> 14:24.287
I'M IN THE TURTLE…
A PERSON IS BLOCKING
THE ONLY EXIT.

14:24.371 --> 14:27.248
I DO NOT RECOGNIZE HIM.
I CANNOT LEAVE UNNOTICED.
WHAT DO I DO?

14:26.039 --> 14:27.269
You don't recognize him?

14:27.374 --> 14:29.751
Then that must be the new guy.

14:29.793 --> 14:32.837
Well, if he finds you, then you
have no choice but to eliminate.

14:32.837 --> 14:35.297
UNDERSTOOD.
I WILL ELIMINATE THE ROOKIE
OCCUPYING SPACE BY THE EXIT.

14:35.465 --> 14:39.218
But quietly is the operative word.
The others must not find you.

14:39.761 --> 14:41.637
Holding on to Trish is everything.

14:42.097 --> 14:45.642
I'll have them head
over there as well, just in case.

15:10.625 --> 15:12.668
I could've sworn
there was something there…

15:12.710 --> 15:14.253
…and you were correct.

15:14.838 --> 15:17.215
Heads up… It's happening…
Something's trying to atta—

15:21.052 --> 15:24.013
<i>Something removed… my throat?!</i>

15:27.809 --> 15:29.268
Mista, couldja try to…

15:29.436 --> 15:31.104
Get off my back, okay?!

15:31.771 --> 15:32.938
Is something wrong?

15:32.981 --> 15:35.608
Nah. Giorno's just waving to us.

15:35.650 --> 15:39.362
I'm sure Bucciarati just wants us
to hurry up and pick out a car.

15:39.404 --> 15:41.239
Look, everyone can just
take a chill pill!

15:41.239 --> 15:44.992
MISSION ACCOMPLISHED…
ALL IS QUIET,
NOW THAT I HAVE HIS THROAT.

15:42.657 --> 15:44.992
Di motto! Glorious!

15:51.583 --> 15:55.753
<i>What the hell? There's nothing left
of the cabinet, and still no Stand?</i>

15:55.837 --> 16:00.337
<i>And why am I not able to
see it when it attacks me?</i>

16:00.383 --> 16:01.467
<i>Howie he hiding from me?</i>

16:01.509 --> 16:03.302
<i>Howie he dislodging
pieces of my body?</i>

16:03.595 --> 16:05.888
<i>Dislodging… He must be…</i>

16:07.223 --> 16:09.058
SHPANG

16:09.184 --> 16:11.561
So you managed to dislodge sections
of his leg and eye, too?

16:11.603 --> 16:15.732
Di motto! Wonderful…
Now come to papa, Babyhead!

16:15.732 --> 16:18.067
MISSION NOT ACCOMPLISHED…
AS YOU COULD GUESS,
I'VE BEEN FIGURED OUT…
WHAT NOW?

16:19.194 --> 16:20.695
What?

16:21.154 --> 16:22.488
THE NEW GUY TOOK THE KEY FROM
THE BACK OF THAT TURTLE.

16:22.530 --> 16:24.573
IT SEEMS REMOVING HE KEY ALLOWS
ONLY LIVING ORGANISMS TO EXIT.

16:25.074 --> 16:26.909
MY BODY KEEPS RISING
HIGHER AND HIGHER…
WHAT DO I DO NOW?

16:27.035 --> 16:29.579
Sorry, I'm not following
what you're saying…

16:29.662 --> 16:31.080
Living organism?

16:31.164 --> 16:32.248
You're a Stand!

16:32.332 --> 16:34.625
The rules of the living
and the dead don't apply to you.

16:34.667 --> 16:37.002
THAT IS CERTAINLY TRUE,
BUT I STILL HAVE THE EYE
I DISLODGED FROM HIM…
THAT EYE IS ALIVE.

16:39.881 --> 16:42.633
<i>I knew it… It was that cabinet.</i>

16:53.144 --> 16:54.436
<i>I see now…</i>

16:55.230 --> 16:57.273
<i>It's not that
I couldn't see my attacker.</i>

16:57.398 --> 16:59.483
<i>I was looking at him
this entire time!</i>

16:59.567 --> 17:02.152
<i>He attacks by disassembling
the human body</i>

17:02.237 --> 17:04.489
<i>and then rearranging the pieces
into something else entirely!</i>

17:04.489 --> 17:06.199
MELONE.
WHAT SHOULD I DO?
WHAT SHOULD I DO?
WHAT SHOULD I DO?

17:06.199 --> 17:07.283
Don't panic!

17:07.367 --> 17:10.286
What difference does it make
at this point anyway?

17:10.370 --> 17:12.622
That hot shot rookie hasn't
been breathing for a while now,

17:12.705 --> 17:13.831
and he's missing a leg to boot.

17:13.915 --> 17:17.710
Just get rid of him and
grab the turtle so you have Trish!

17:17.919 --> 17:18.920
Roger.

17:20.588 --> 17:21.964
Golden Wind!

17:25.843 --> 17:27.886
<i>So it splits itself apart to dodge!</i>

17:28.179 --> 17:29.346
<i>Which means…</i>

17:41.067 --> 17:42.568
G-Guys…

17:43.194 --> 17:45.196
I need to somehow… let them know…

17:48.950 --> 17:49.992
<i>I think I got him!</i>

17:50.034 --> 17:52.661
Nope, that there is just
your standard rock.

17:57.792 --> 17:59.794
<i>Sh-Shit…</i>

17:59.836 --> 18:01.796
<i>He's gonna swipe Trish…</i>

18:01.921 --> 18:05.132
<i>At this rate,
he's gonna kill Bucciarati!</i>

18:08.720 --> 18:10.096
<i>He's got power…</i>

18:10.763 --> 18:13.515
<i>What's this guy's weakness?</i>

18:27.822 --> 18:30.366
I will leave the neophyte's body
here before fleeing.

18:30.867 --> 18:32.159
Just as I planned,

18:32.201 --> 18:36.288
the girl is totally mine,
and no one is the wiser.

18:36.414 --> 18:38.332
Di motto! Good!

18:40.752 --> 18:44.714
I will see you very soon, Melone.
Wait for me on the train.

18:49.177 --> 18:52.555
So he rearranges the human body
into other objects…

18:52.597 --> 18:56.684
Your powers just gave me
a fantastic idea.

18:57.185 --> 19:01.230
They're not all that different
from Golden Wind.

19:02.899 --> 19:06.569
We both have the power to
create something new.

19:07.028 --> 19:08.738
You've taught me a lot,

19:08.821 --> 19:11.907
and pushed me
to the absolute brink.

19:12.033 --> 19:13.451
I think you actually…

19:14.160 --> 19:16.078
pushed me to be better.

19:16.996 --> 19:19.581
M-Melone, are you listening?

19:20.041 --> 19:21.751
It completely slipped my mind,

19:21.834 --> 19:24.962
but I learned how
the new guy's power works now.

19:25.046 --> 19:26.589
What about the new guy?

19:31.010 --> 19:33.429
- The button is now an eyeball…
- Hey, Babyhead,

19:33.471 --> 19:34.889
- Right in the palm of his hand,
- what are you talking about?

19:34.931 --> 19:36.557
- It transformed into an eyeball.
- What's this about the dead newbie?

19:36.557 --> 19:40.602
RUMBLE

19:36.724 --> 19:39.643
He placed it into the socket!

19:39.727 --> 19:40.624
He did the same
with his throat and leg!

19:41.896 --> 19:44.273
He has the power to
make living things!

19:44.315 --> 19:46.400
He made his own body parts!

19:46.442 --> 19:48.444
He's the opposite of me!

19:48.486 --> 19:50.946
Hey, who the hell are
you talking about?

19:51.989 --> 19:54.783
Nice try! Golden Wind!

19:56.244 --> 19:58.537
The newbie… He…

19:59.122 --> 20:01.040
He's back to life and after me!

20:02.709 --> 20:05.128
A-Are you listening, Melone?

20:05.211 --> 20:08.714
He transformed part of the bike
into some kind of seed!

20:08.756 --> 20:09.965
I'm totally stuck!

20:10.049 --> 20:12.092
I have to get rid of
the parts that are stuck!

20:12.135 --> 20:14.428
I need to get away from the bike!

20:24.897 --> 20:27.608
He did it again… Another rock?

20:28.317 --> 20:30.527
<i>Dammit, he's after the turtle.</i>

20:30.611 --> 20:32.988
<i>I'll stop him dead in his tracks!</i>

20:33.156 --> 20:35.032
Simmer down now, Babyhead!

20:35.116 --> 20:37.159
Let him pick up the turtle.

20:37.243 --> 20:38.827
<i>What do you mean?</i>

20:38.953 --> 20:41.246
Just wait for him to pick up the turtle,

20:41.289 --> 20:43.749
then eviscerate him till
there's nothing left.

20:43.916 --> 20:46.209
<i>The bike's spewing oil now…
What now?!</i>

20:46.461 --> 20:49.338
Hurt him so bad he'll never be able
to revive himself!

20:59.557 --> 21:00.766
I got him!

21:01.601 --> 21:02.685
I'll give credit.

21:02.769 --> 21:05.646
You actually managed to
spook me a bit, you bastard!

21:05.688 --> 21:06.855
Now, get ready for some pain
because you're about to

21:06.898 --> 21:07.899
watch me rip off your hea—

21:07.982 --> 21:11.235
Your talent for transforming
human bodies into objects

21:11.319 --> 21:12.862
really inspired something in me.

21:13.863 --> 21:15.948
Maybe it was fate,

21:15.990 --> 21:18.534
or maybe it was
our similar abilities

21:18.576 --> 21:20.578
that ultimately drew us together.

21:20.661 --> 21:21.870
But thanks to you
and your influence,

21:21.913 --> 21:25.166
Golden Wind is
a whole lot more capable.

21:25.208 --> 21:27.210
W-Where did it go?

21:27.293 --> 21:30.296
I just tore off your wrist.
Where did it go?

21:30.338 --> 21:32.256
Tore off?

21:32.340 --> 21:33.758
Sorry, but you're incorrect.

21:34.175 --> 21:36.468
I chose to let it go on purpose.

21:36.552 --> 21:39.096
I'll do you a big favor
and give you some advice.

21:39.180 --> 21:42.516
You would best be served
by using your hand

21:42.558 --> 21:45.018
to keep yourself from harm
instead of trying to harm me.

21:45.061 --> 21:47.605
You can shove that advice
up your ass!

21:47.730 --> 21:48.731
Die!

21:49.941 --> 21:50.942
What?!

21:52.360 --> 21:56.572
My severed hand is already
another organism.

21:56.697 --> 21:58.407
It's eagerly devouring you
from the inside out.

21:59.492 --> 22:00.493
Yes.

22:03.788 --> 22:06.123
Exactly, it's a piranha!

23:38.466 --> 23:41.969
EPISODE 18
VERSO VENEZIA!
